MyPLC/MyPLC_IO_Modbus.cpp: W906_PlcM1SDoorDebounce (end of file) runs on every model-1 frame inside W906_PlcM1SFill, before
W906_PlcM1SAllDoors (same line). A door bit of golden's iSafeDoor[] list on the PLC (ISABase 4) that reads 0 is held at 1 until
it has read 0 on every frame for g_w906PlcDoorOpenMs = 500 ms; 1 passes at once and clears the timer. Port 310 (all doors,
WAR16125) is made from the held bits, so it gets the same 0.5 s. EMG (Port 300) and all other bits untouched.
Done at the data layer, not in CheckSafeDoorIsClosed: that one is also called once by START / a manual move / the tray clamp,
where a timer would let a really open door pass.

tests/test_myplc_modbus.cpp: [5] (mapping, frame by frame) runs with 0 ms; new [8] through the real PLCIOTaskCycle path in real
time: one-frame flicker held, 250 ms held, flicker clears the timer, 600 ms open -> 0 and Port 310 = 0, closing at once, EMG
passed. 83 passed / 0 failed. Code-after-comment scan 0. wb_serve compiled; its link waits for EastSun's running program.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
